              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Roe"} John Roe
              %em Lectures on operator K-theory and the Atiyah-Singer Index Theorem
              (2004) (
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/rognes/higson/Book.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A lightning review of the proof is on the last pages of
          %ul
            %li#Introduction
              %em> Introduction to KK-theory and E-theory
              , Lecture notes (Lisbon 2009) (
              %a{:href => "http://oaa.ist.utl.pt/files/cursos/courseD_Lecture4_KK_and_E1.pdf"}> pdf slides
              )
          %h3#ReferencesPhysics From the point of view of physics
          %p
            The index theorem has an interpretation in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
            on the given space. See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics#RelationToIndexTheory"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
          %p Traditional physics arguments along these lines include for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                P. Windey,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric quantum mechanics and the Atiyah–Singer index theorem
                %strong B15
                (1984). (
                %a{:href => "http://th-www.if.uj.edu.pl/~acta/vol15/pdf/v15p0435.pdf"}> PDF
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alvarez-Gaum%C3%A9"}> Luis Alvarez-Gaumé
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and the Atiyah-Singer index theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103940278"} EUCLID
            %li
              %p
                Florian Hanisch, Matthias Ludewig,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Rigorous Construction of the Supersymmetric Path Integral Associated to a Compact Spin Manifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.10027"} arXiv:1709.10027
